rationalPoints -- Compute all of the rational points of an affine variety
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        l = rationalPoints I
  * Inputs:
      * I, which is an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, contained in a
        polynomial ring over a finite field.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * UseGB => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false,  turns on and off a Groebner basis computation of the ideal.
        Default is false.
      * UseMinGens => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false,  turns on and off a mingens computation of the ideal that
        may change the chosen generators.
      * SortGens => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false,  sorts generators in order to make searching for zeroes
        more efficient.
      * LowMem => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false,  uses an alternative algorithm that is slower but much less
        memory intensive.
      * Amount => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false,  output changes to the number of zeroes.
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, output includes the generators of the ideal that the computation
        uses. These may be modified by UseGB or UseMinGens
  * Outputs:
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of lists. Each internal
        list is an n-tuple of elements of the finite field such that the
        n-tuple represents a point in Affine n-space lying on the variety
        defined by the input ideal I.

